{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "commonjs",
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
```

5. Scroll down, add commit message: "Fix tsconfig for Node.js"
6. Click **"Commit changes"**

---

## **Key Changes:**

✅ Added `"types": ["node"]` - This tells TypeScript to include Node.js types (including `console`)  
✅ Changed `"lib": ["ES2020"]` - Removed DOM library (not needed for backend)

---

## **Step 2: Render Will Auto-Redeploy**

1. Go back to your Render dashboard
2. Render automatically detects the GitHub change
3. It will **automatically redeploy** (takes 2-3 minutes)
4. Watch the logs for progress

---

## **If It Doesn't Auto-Deploy:**

1. In Render dashboard, click your service
2. Click **"Manual Deploy"** → **"Deploy latest commit"**

---

